From e3fda1a31ddcada434e150402fc4cc673a708d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] power: supply: apple_j71t_charger: this cell charges
 above 4.2 V

The battery safety window ended at 4.2 V. This unit's cell is full above
that: iOS reports 4256-4274 mV at 100 % (2026-10-27 capture), and Linux
read 4249 mV at 98 % while charging. Near full, every guard pass returned
-ERANGE, the policy restored the 100 mA handoff, the voltage sagged, and
charging resumed 30 s later: "charging policy stepped down: -34" every
30 s with the Mac cable, and after 15 s at 2100 mA with the camera adapter.

The PMIC owns charge voltage and termination; the window only rejects
implausible gauge samples. Raise the ceiling to 4.4 V.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
index 923ad579b4..b96d071302 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
@@ -32,6 +32,15 @@
 #define J71T_SAMPLE_GRACE_MS 60000
 #define J71T_FAULT_RETRY_MS 60000
 #define J71T_OWNER_RETRY_MS 30000
+/*
+ * Battery sanity window. This unit's cell charges above 4.2 V: iOS reports
+ * 4256-4274 mV at 100 % (2026-10-27 capture) and Linux saw 4249 mV at 98 %
+ * while charging. With a 4.2 V ceiling the policy stopped charging near full
+ * every 30 s. The PMIC owns charge voltage and termination; this window only
+ * rejects implausible gauge samples.
+ */
+#define J71T_VBAT_MIN_UV 3000000
+#define J71T_VBAT_MAX_UV 4400000
 
 static const int j71t_budgets_ua[] = { 500000, 1000000, 2100000, 2400000 };
 
@@ -259,7 +268,7 @@ static int j71t_battery_safe(struct j71t_charger *charger)
 	ret = power_supply_get_property(battery, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW, &value);
 	if (ret)
 		goto transient;
-	if (value.intval < 3000000 || value.intval > 4200000) {
+	if (value.intval < J71T_VBAT_MIN_UV || value.intval > J71T_VBAT_MAX_UV) {
 		ret = -ERANGE;
 		goto out;
 	}
